rounds.content:
{
  "proposal": [
    {
      "title": "__VOR-019_SubI_NDI-Asset-Preflight-And-Missing-Asset-Evidence",
      "body": "Parent-Issue: #107; feeds into #651 and #653.\n\nBeschreibung: Add a small, reproducible preflight/check command for the NDI/asset-availability gate before the full manual NDI end-to-end test. The task should verify NDI runtime/library availability where detectable, required media/test assets, and missing-asset behavior without requiring a live production show setup.\n\nAcceptance-Evidence:\n- A documented command runs the NDI/asset preflight locally.\n- The command writes a machine-readable JSON report with passed/failed/skipped checks.\n- Missing NDI runtime, missing sample media, or unavailable optional dependencies produce explicit actionable failures, not ambiguous panics.\n- At least one automated test or fixture covers missing-asset handling.\n- #107 can link the report as pre-E2E evidence; ROADMAP QA status is not changed by the agent.",
      "labels": [
        "priority: high",
        "testing",
        "automation"
      ],
      "agent": "gemini_cli"
    },
    {
      "title": "__VOR-020_SubI_Release-Artifact-Manifest-And-Start-Sanity-Command",
      "body": "Parent-Issue: #652; feeds into #651 and #653.\n\nBeschreibung: Add a narrow packaging sanity command that proves a release artifact can be located or built, records its commit/version/path, and performs a bounded start sanity check. This should not try to solve all installer/signing work; it creates repeatable evidence for the packaging gate.\n\nAcceptance-Evidence:\n- One documented command produces a release-artifact manifest JSON containing commit SHA, target platform, build/profile, artifact path, and timestamp.\n- The command fails clearly if the artifact is missing or version metadata cannot be determined.\n- A bounded start sanity check confirms the binary starts far enough to avoid an immediate panic/crash loop, then exits or is killed cleanly.\n- Logs are written to a predictable ignored artifact folder.\n- #652 can link the manifest/logs as install/start-sanity evidence; ROADMAP QA status is not changed by the agent.",
      "labels": [
        "priority: high",
        "testing",
        "automation"
      ],
      "agent": "kiro_cli"
    },
    {
      "title": "__VOR-021_SubI_Timeline-Persist-Reload-Dirty-State-Acceptance-Fixture",
      "body": "Parent-Issue: #662; relates to #661, #96, #103, and #651.\n\nBeschreibung: Add one focused deterministic acceptance fixture for the Timeline/Show-Control matrix: create or load a minimal timeline/cue state, save it, reload it, and verify persisted fields plus dirty-state transitions. This is intentionally smaller than the full Timeline MVP and should produce concrete evidence for the acceptance matrix.\n\nAcceptance-Evidence:\n- A documented test or command creates a minimal timeline/cue/project state without manual UI input.\n- Save/reload preserves the relevant timeline/cue data checked by the fixture.\n- Dirty-state changes are asserted before save, after save, and after reload/project switch where supported.\n- The test produces logs or a test artifact that can be linked from #662.\n- Any unsupported behavior is reported as failed or explicitly inconclusive, not silently skipped; ROADMAP QA status is not changed by the agent.",
      "labels": [
        "priority: high",
        "testing"
      ],
      "agent": "claude_code"
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": "Ich habe keine Master-Issues als Coding-Tasks vorgeschlagen. #650/#547/#548/#549 sind bereits offen und enthalten den UI-Harness/Smoke-Umfang, daher waere ein weiterer UI-Smoke-Task wahrscheinlich redundant. Cluster/Multi-Instance (#654-#659) ist derzeit vor allem eine Scope- und Produktentscheidung; ohne klare 1.0-Entscheidung waeren neue Coding-Issues dort riskant. Die drei Vorschlaege sind klein, delegierbar und liefern konkrete Release-1.0-Evidenz fuer #107, #652 und #662/#661. Agent-Zuordnung: jules wurde bewusst nicht gewaehlt, weil diese Vorschlaege keine grossen UI-Refactorings sind; lokale CLI-Agents passen besser fuer isolierte Preflight-, Packaging- und Rust-Testarbeiten.",
  "risks": [
    "NDI-Verfuegbarkeit kann plattform- oder runtime-abhaengig sein; der Preflight darf den echten End-to-End-Test aus #107 nicht ersetzen.",
    "Packaging-Start-Sanity kann in headless oder GPU-losen Umgebungen instabil sein; der Task muss klare skip/fail-Regeln definieren.",
    "Timeline-Persistenz kann bestehende Architekturgrenzen beruehren; der Fixture sollte klein bleiben und keine grosse Timeline-Refaktorierung ausloesen."
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}

